# R_TRIG and F_TRIG with CLK = TRUE from the first evaluation, period 100 ms.
#
# Derivation (ed.3 table 43 / ed.2 table 35 bodies):
#   R_TRIG: Q := CLK AND NOT M; M := CLK;         with M initially FALSE
#   F_TRIG: Q := NOT CLK AND NOT M; M := NOT CLK; with M initially TRUE
#           (ed.3) or FALSE (FDIS 2001)
# With CLK = TRUE on the first evaluation, R_TRIG reports a rising edge
# (M was FALSE) and F_TRIG reports nothing whatever its initial M, since
# NOT CLK is FALSE. From then on both are in a defined state, so this
# trace holds under either edition, unlike edge/f_trig cycle 0.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: clk
outputs: qr qf
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.6.3.5.2 table 43 (R_TRIG, F_TRIG bodies)
---
# first evaluation with CLK TRUE: a rising edge, no falling edge
0 clk=TRUE  => qr=TRUE  qf=FALSE
1           => qr=FALSE qf=FALSE
2 clk=FALSE => qr=FALSE qf=TRUE
3           => qr=FALSE qf=FALSE
4 clk=TRUE  => qr=TRUE  qf=FALSE
5 clk=FALSE => qr=FALSE qf=TRUE
